      "section": "Fusion structure",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "Six oncogenic fusions, each drawn as its two partners end to end: one lane per partner, one bar per protein domain, a dotted seam at the breakpoint. Bar fill is the fraction of the domain the fusion keeps, so a lost domain is an empty outline. The x axis is an ordinal domain slot, not an amino-acid position.\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/advanced_viz_demo"
    },
